### 4. embodied-schemas#83 -- Fix Jetson Thor + Orin Nano memory_bus_bits (closes ES#8)

Two-line YAML fix. Both Jetsons had `memory_bus_bits` inconsistent
with `memory_bandwidth_gbps`:

| File | Before | After | Math check |
|---|---|---|---|
| `thor_gpu_128gb_lpddr5x.yaml` | 512 | **256** | 273 / 8.533 = 256 |
| `orin_nano_gpu_8gb_lpddr5.yaml` | 64 | **128** | 68 / 4.267 = 128 |

NVIDIA's published specs both confirm the corrected values. A 512-bit
Thor at LPDDR5X-8533 would deliver 545 GB/s (2× spec); a 64-bit Orin
Nano at LPDDR5-4267 would deliver 34 GB/s (½ spec). Bandwidth values
themselves were correct and unchanged.

This bug was originally discovered while backfilling the consumer-side
PhysicalSpec in graphs#139; the fix was carried as `KNOWN_OVERRIDES`
entries in `physical_spec_loader.py` pending this upstream fix.

962/962 full repo pass.

