### 6. graphs#249 -- #132 closer (propagation contract + coverage pin)

Audit revealed that issue #132 ("Switch PhysicalSpec source from
inline factories to embodied-schemas ComputeProduct loader") was
**functionally complete**. The broader campaign across #130/#234/
#241/#245 had already eliminated every inline `PhysicalSpec(...)`
constructor (0 left outside the loader). 43 of 47 registered mappers
source PhysicalSpec from the loader; the 4 unpopulated SKUs are the
data-availability tail per DECISION-2026-05-21-001 Question B.

The one remaining exit criterion was an explicit propagation regression
test. PR #249 delivered it.

New tests in `tests/hardware/test_physical_spec_loader.py`:

**`TestYamlPropagationContract`** -- synthesizes a YAML in tmp_path,
points `EMBODIED_SCHEMAS_DATA_DIR` at it, asserts the loader returns
the values written. Then mutates the YAML on disk, asserts a second
call returns the new values. Pins the live-propagation contract with
no stale-cache path.

**`TestPhysicalSpecCoveragePin`** -- pins 43 populated / 4 unpopulated
(ARM Mali-G78, AmpereOne-1core-ref, Snapdragon Ride, DFM-128 named
explicitly). Regression test against future factory refactors that
accidentally drop `physical_spec` wiring.

1250/1250 tests/hardware/ pass (+3 net).

## Key decisions

- **Single-virtual-die approximation retired** (closing the long-pending
  Question A in DECISION-2026-05-21-001). All 3 AMD chiplet datacenter
  SKUs now use the v13 multi-die representation. Intel Xeon tile
  architectures stay single-die per the original design call (tile-
  internal IO; no separate IOD silicon).

- **Shared-IOD pattern established**: when a SKU reuses an existing
  IOD die unchanged (Bergamo + Genoa share `genoa_iod`), the YAML
  copies the IO die block verbatim with the same canonical
  `die_id`. Pinned by cross-SKU shared-IOD invariant tests.

- **Distinct-IOD pattern established**: when a SKU introduces new
  IOD silicon (Turin Dense), it uses a new `die_id` (`turin_iod`)
  with distinct field values where the silicon actually differs
  (memory BW, CXL version, transistor count, idle power). Same
  family (coherence topology, security processor, PCIe gen)
  validated. Pinned by cross-SKU distinct-IOD invariant tests.

- **CI pin bump pattern rehearsed**: now done twice in this session
  (PR #247 and PR #248). Standard recipe: bump SHA, extend history
  comment block, update all 8 ref sites across 3 workflow files.

